      "tip": "Bengali has no 'a' or 'the' — it uses **classifiers** instead:\n\n- **একটা আম** (*ekta am*) — *a* mango (number + -টা)\n- **আমটা** (*amta*) — *the* mango (noun + -টা)\n- **আমগুলো** (*amgulo*) — *the* mangoes (noun + -গুলো)\n\nSo putting **-টা** *after* the noun makes it specific, like 'the'. Putting it on a *number* gives 'a / one'.\n\n**-টি** (*-ti*) is the more formal or written version (**একটি আম**); it also sounds a bit gentle or affectionate, and Kolkata speakers use it more. **-গুলি** is the written version of -গুলো.\n\nBangladesh is mango heaven: summer brings dozens of varieties like *Langra*, *Himsagar* and *Fazli*.",
